.TH TIDE-TERMINAL 1 "November 2026" "Tide Terminal 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
tide-terminal \- native terminal with input alerts and command timers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tide-terminal
.RI [ gui ] " [options]"
.br
.B tide-terminal
.RB [ --working-directory " directory] [" --hold "] " -e
.I command " [arguments ...]"
.br
.B tide-terminal run
.RI [ options ] " -- command [arguments ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tide is a GPU-rendered Linux terminal with Bash, Zsh and Fish integration,
command history, prompt alerts, timers and captured-output follow-ups.
Without a command it starts the shell selected in its preferences.
.SH DESKTOP OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -e ", " --execute
Run the remaining arguments directly in the terminal. Arguments are not joined
or interpreted by a shell. To run shell syntax, use an explicit shell and -c.
The command's terminal closes on completion; other tabs remain open.
.TP
.B --working-directory directory
Start the terminal in this directory. Invalid directories are rejected.
.TP
.B --hold
Keep an executed command's terminal open after completion.
.TP
.B "gui --gpu integrated|discrete|auto|software"
Override the saved renderer for one launch. Integrated is the default.
.TP
.B "gui --shell path"
Override the saved shell for one launch.
.TP
.B "gui --private"
Disable Tide history for the session.
.SH TIMERS AND APPENDING
.B "T_: 'command' : -s 30"
runs a command with a thirty-second limit. Use -m for minutes and -rex for an
output regular expression. See tide-terminal timer --help for all conditions.
.PP
Inside an integrated Tide shell,
.B "A_: '| grep READY'"
processes the last completed command's captured output without rerunning it.
.B "A_: '>> results.txt'"
appends captured output to a file. Use 1>> or 2>> to select stdout or stderr
when separate capture is available.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.tide.toml
Preferences: renderer, shell, font, opacity, alerts and privacy.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tide-terminal/history.sqlite3
Command history, unless XDG_DATA_HOME selects another data directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B TIDE_CONFIG
selects an alternate preferences file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tide-terminal
tide-terminal --working-directory /tmp
tide-terminal -e htop
tide-terminal --hold -e bash -c 'printf "hello\\n"'
T_: 'sleep 60' : -s 3
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR fish (1),
.BR zsh (1)
